 "notes": "Combined lower envelope of the two 95% C.L. observed constraints on |d_me| from Fig. 2 (right panel) of arXiv:2312.13723v2: 'GPS (this work)' (Rb GPS satellite clocks vs H-maser, 1.8e-19 to 7.1e-17 eV, the stronger bound where it exists) and 'Cavities (this work)' (NPL/PTB 2220 km fiber-linked cavity comparison, 1e-19 to 2.1e-15 eV). Extracted from the raster panel of the e-print figure combined.pdf by color masking of the boundary lines (GPS RGB 199,62,4; Cavities coral 255,127,80 incl. its composite 216,81,27 over the GPS fill), with axes calibrated from tick marks (decade ticks at 259.5 px, checked against axis labels). Calibration cross-checked by reproducing the |d_me| floors from the Fig. 1 amplitude limits via Eqs. (11) and (13) (GPS ~1e2, cavities ~1e4.5-1e5). 'Space Clocks (spatial/temporal)' dashed/dotted curves are future projections and were excluded. Paper's convention matches Damour-Donoghue: m_e -> m_e(1 + d_me kappa phi), kappa = sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl (Eqs. 2-3). Stochastic-field correction (xi ~ 1/3) already included by the paper; rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed.",
